{ No pip after creating a new environment with a specific python version (?)

  Once, it seemed I had no pip anymore after installing a new environment. However, I was unable to reproduce this behavior with the follwoing command: 
code {
(base) $ conda create -n renes-modules python=3.14
(base) $ conda activate renes-modules
code }

  No more pip (not anymore)
code {
(renes-modules) $ which pip
code }

  pip needs to be installed:
code {
(renes-modules) $ conda install pip
code }

}
